  "Question": "It is given that \\(x\\) varies directly as \\(y\\) and inversely as the square of \\(z,\\) and that \\(x=10\\) when \\(y=4\\) and \\(z=14.\\) Then, when \\(y=16\\) and \\(z=7,\\) \\(x\\) equals:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(180\\)",
    "B": "\\(160\\)",
    "C": "\\(154\\)",
    "D": "\\(140\\)",
    "E": "\\(120\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Compare the changes one quantity at a time. With \\(z\\) fixed, direct variation means that changing \\(y\\) from \\(4\\) to \\(16\\) multiplies \\(x\\) by \\(16/4=4\\).\n\nChanging \\(z\\) from \\(14\\) to \\(7\\) halves \\(z\\), so its square becomes one-fourth as large. Since \\(x\\) varies inversely as \\(z^2\\), this multiplies \\(x\\) by another \\(4\\). Therefore,\n\\[\nx=10\\cdot4\\cdot4=160.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(160\\), choice B.",
